## Analytics

The complete data set behind the [Analytics dashboard](/admin/analytics) — cookie-free, first-party traffic measurement stored in your own database. All endpoints are `GET`, require authentication and return JSON.

| Method | URL | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET | `/api/analytics` | Full report (every section at once) |
| GET | `/api/analytics/summary` | Headline KPIs |
| GET | `/api/analytics/timeseries` | Views / visitors / sessions over time |
| GET | `/api/analytics/breakdowns` | Every dimension table |
| GET | `/api/analytics/breakdowns/{dimension}` | A single dimension table |
| GET | `/api/analytics/heatmap` | Weekday × hour matrix |
| GET | `/api/analytics/realtime` | Traffic in the last N minutes |

> **Note:** If the built-in analytics is switched off (`ANALYTICS_ENABLED=false`) or the database is unavailable, every endpoint answers `503`.

### Query parameters

The period and filters are interpreted identically by every endpoint.

| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `range` | string | `7d` | `today`, `yesterday`, `24h`, `7d`, `28d`, `30d`, `90d`, `mtd`, `ytd`, `12mo`, `custom` |
| `from` | date | — | `YYYY-MM-DD`, with `range=custom` |
| `to` | date | — | `YYYY-MM-DD`, inclusive |
| `granularity` | string | auto | `hour`, `day` or `month` — overrides the bucket size |
| `compare` | boolean | `true` | `false` skips the previous-period aggregations |
| `limit` | integer | `15` | Rows per breakdown table, max `500` |
| `minutes` | integer | `30` | Realtime endpoint only, max `180` |

**Filters** — any combination, all exact matches:

| Parameter | Values |
| --- | --- |
| `page_type` | `home`, `article`, `category`, `author`, `tag`, `search`, `page`, `forum`, `marketplace`, `webshop`, `other` |
| `path` | Exact URL path, e.g. `/article/rtx-5090-teszt` |
| `channel` | `direct`, `organic`, `social`, `referral`, `campaign`, `internal`, `ai` |
| `device` | `desktop`, `mobile`, `tablet` |
| `country` | ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code, e.g. `HU` |
| `ref_host` | Referrer host, e.g. `google.hu` |
| `category` | Category name |
| `author` | Author name |

A filter applies to *every* section of the response: summary, time series, breakdowns and heatmap. An unknown `range` silently falls back to `7d`.

### Full report

Everything in one request: summary, previous period, time series, all breakdowns and the heatmap. This is the most expensive endpoint — use the section endpoints when you need only one part.

```http
GET /api/analytics?range=28d&channel=organic&limit=20
```

**Response (abridged):**

```json
{
  "range": {
    "key":           "28d",
    "from":          "2026-06-29T00:00:00+02:00",
    "to":            "2026-07-27T00:00:00+02:00",
    "previous_from": "2026-06-01T00:00:00+02:00",
    "previous_to":   "2026-06-29T00:00:00+02:00",
    "granularity":   "day",
    "timezone":      "Europe/Budapest"
  },
  "filter":  { "channel": "organic" },
  "summary": { <summary object> },
  "previous":{ <summary object> },
  "series":         [ { "bucket": "2026-06-29", "views": 2612, "visitors": 1620, "sessions": 1854 } ],
  "previous_series":[ { "bucket": "2026-06-01", "views": 2280, "visitors": 1410, "sessions": 1602 } ],
  "breakdowns":     { "pages": [...], "channels": [...], "referrers": [...], ... },
  "heatmap":        [ { "weekday": 2, "hour": 9, "views": 187 } ]
}
```

> **Note:** Sections that were not requested are **absent** from the JSON rather than empty. `range` and `filter` are always present. With `compare=false` the `previous`, `previous_series`, `range.previous_from` and `range.previous_to` fields are omitted.

**curl:**

```bash
curl -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" "{{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/analytics?range=28d"
```

### Summary

The headline KPIs plus the same numbers for the previous period. Fastest endpoint.

```http
GET /api/analytics/summary?range=today&compare=false
```

```json
{
  "range":   { "key": "today", "granularity": "hour", "timezone": "Europe/Budapest", ... },
  "filter":  {},
  "summary": {
    "views":             1204,
    "visitors":          812,
    "sessions":          903,
    "views_per_session": 1.3333,
    "avg_engagement_ms": 88000,
    "bounce_rate":       44.2,
    "engagement_rate":   55.8,
    "outbound":          31
  }
}
```

| Field | Type | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `views` | integer | Page views |
| `visitors` | integer | Unique visitors (see the note below) |
| `sessions` | integer | Visits; 30 minutes of inactivity starts a new one |
| `views_per_session` | float | `views / sessions` |
| `avg_engagement_ms` | integer | Average time actually spent on the page, in milliseconds |
| `bounce_rate` | float | Percentage of single-page sessions without engagement |
| `engagement_rate` | float | Percentage of sessions longer than 10s or scrolled past 50% |
| `outbound` | integer | Outbound link clicks and downloads |

> **Warning:** **Reading `visitors`:** the visitor identifier is a hash salted with a key that is regenerated every day, so the same person receives a new identifier each day. Over a multi-day range `visitors` is therefore the *sum of daily uniques*, not the true unique count for the period. This is the price of consent-free, cookie-less measurement; `sessions` and `views` are exact.

### Time series

Bucket size is chosen automatically (`hour` up to 48 hours, `day` up to 120 days, `month` above that) and can be overridden with `granularity`.

| Granularity | Bucket format | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `hour` | `YYYY-MM-DDTHH` | `2026-07-27T14` |
| `day` | `YYYY-MM-DD` | `2026-07-27` |
| `month` | `YYYY-MM` | `2026-07` |

```http
GET /api/analytics/timeseries?range=90d&granularity=month&compare=false
```

```json
{
  "range":  { "key": "90d", "granularity": "month", "timezone": "Europe/Budapest", ... },
  "filter": {},
  "series": [
    { "bucket": "2026-05", "views": 41200, "visitors": 25600, "sessions": 29100 },
    { "bucket": "2026-06", "views": 44870, "visitors": 27340, "sessions": 31020 }
  ]
}
```

Buckets are in the `ANALYTICS_TIMEZONE` local time, and **only buckets with traffic are returned** — fill the gaps with zeroes client-side if you draw a continuous chart.

### Breakdowns

Without a dimension every table is returned at once; with one, only that table.

| Dimension | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| `pages` | Most viewed pages (`key` = path, `label` = page title) |
| `entry_pages` | Landing pages — first page of each session |
| `exit_pages` | Exit pages — last page of each session |
| `channels` | GA4-style default channel grouping |
| `referrers` | Referrer hosts (`label` = recognised brand name) |
| `utm_sources`, `utm_mediums`, `utm_campaigns` | Campaign parameters |
| `devices`, `browsers`, `os` | Technology |
| `countries`, `languages` | Geography (country needs a CDN country header) |
| `page_types`, `categories`, `authors` | Editorial performance |
| `outbound` | Outbound links and downloads (`key` = target URL) |

**Row object:**

| Field | Type | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `key` | string | Raw dimension value — pass it back as a filter |
| `label` | string | Display name when one exists, otherwise empty |
| `views` | integer | Page views |
| `visitors` | integer | Unique visitors — **session count** for entry/exit pages |
| `avg_engagement_ms` | integer | Average time on page in milliseconds |
| `bounce_rate` | float | Percentage; only meaningful for `entry_pages` and `exit_pages`, `0` elsewhere |

```http
GET /api/analytics/breakdowns/referrers?range=7d&limit=5
```

```json
{
  "range":     { "key": "7d", "granularity": "day", "timezone": "Europe/Budapest", ... },
  "filter":    {},
  "dimension": "referrers",
  "rows": [
    { "key": "google.hu",    "label": "Google",   "views": 6120, "visitors": 4284, "avg_engagement_ms": 100000, "bounce_rate": 0 },
    { "key": "facebook.com", "label": "Facebook", "views": 2410, "visitors": 1687, "avg_engagement_ms": 62000,  "bounce_rate": 0 },
    { "key": "chatgpt.com",  "label": "ChatGPT",  "views": 410,  "visitors": 287,  "avg_engagement_ms": 154000, "bounce_rate": 0 }
  ]
}
```

**How did people find one specific article?**

```bash
curl -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" \
  "{{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/analytics/breakdowns/channels?range=7d&path=/article/rtx-5090-teszt"
```

An unknown dimension name returns `404` listing the valid names.

### Heatmap

Traffic by weekday and hour. Only non-zero cells are returned.

```http
GET /api/analytics/heatmap?range=90d
```

```json
{
  "range":   { "key": "90d", "timezone": "Europe/Budapest", ... },
  "filter":  {},
  "heatmap": [
    { "weekday": 2, "hour": 9,  "views": 187 },
    { "weekday": 2, "hour": 10, "views": 204 }
  ]
}
```

| Field | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `weekday` | `1` = Sunday … `7` = Saturday (MongoDB `$dayOfWeek` convention) |
| `hour` | `0`–`23` in the `ANALYTICS_TIMEZONE` local time |
| `views` | Page views in that weekday + hour cell |

### Realtime

Traffic over the last `minutes` minutes (default 30, max 180). Period and filter parameters do **not** apply to this endpoint.

```http
GET /api/analytics/realtime?minutes=5
```

```json
{
  "minutes":         30,
  "active_visitors": 47,
  "views":           312,
  "per_minute":    [ { "bucket": "2026-07-27T18:41", "views": 9, "visitors": 7, "sessions": 0 } ],
  "top_pages":     [ { "key": "/article/rtx-5090-teszt", "label": "RTX 5090 teszt", "views": 18, "visitors": 12, ... } ],
  "top_channels":  [ { "key": "organic", "label": "organic", "views": 22, "visitors": 15, ... } ],
  "top_countries": [ { "key": "HU", "label": "HU", "views": 41, "visitors": 28, ... } ],
  "devices":       [ { "key": "mobile", "label": "mobile", "views": 28, "visitors": 19, ... } ]
}
```

`per_minute[].bucket` is a **UTC** timestamp in `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM` form, unlike the other endpoints which bucket in local time.

