### Create article

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| POST | `/api/articles` | Required |

**Request body (JSON):**

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `title` | string | Yes | Article title. Slug is auto-generated. |
| `summary` | string | | Short excerpt shown in listings. |
| `content` | string | | Markdown body. |
| `author` | string | | Display name (used when `author_id` is absent). |
| `author_id` | string | | ObjectID of an existing author. |
| `category` | string | | Display name. |
| `category_id` | string | | ObjectID of an existing category. |
| `tags` | string[] | | Tag list. |
| `image_url` | string | | Featured image URL. If S3 is configured, external URLs are auto-imported to the media library. |
| `seo_title` | string | | Optional SEO title (maximum 70 characters). When omitted, `title` is used. |
| `meta_description` | string | | Optional meta description (maximum 160 characters). When omitted, `summary` is used. |
| `image_alt_text` | string | | Optional featured-image alternative text (maximum 150 characters). When omitted, `title` is used. |
| `ai_content_disclosure` | string | Yes | AI declaration for the article content: `none`, `assisted`, or `generated`. For backward compatibility only, omitted values are stored as `none`. |
| `ai_image_disclosure` | string | Yes, if image_url is set | AI declaration for the featured image: `unmodified`, `modified`, or `generated`. For backward compatibility only, an omitted value is stored as `unmodified` when `image_url` is set. |
| `published` | bool | | Publish immediately (default: `false`). |
| `publish_at` | string (RFC3339) | | Scheduled publish time. Null or omit to use the current time when `published=true`. |

**curl:**

```bash
curl -X POST -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "title":      "My New Article",
    "summary":    "A short summary.",
    "content":    "## Introduction\n\nHello world.",
    "category":   "Technology",
    "category_id":"664a000000000000000000bb",
    "tags":       ["go", "tutorial"],
    "ai_content_disclosure": "none",
    "published":  true
  }' \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/articles
```

**Response 201:** the created article object.
**Response 400:** `{"error":"A cím megadása kötelező"}`

### Update article

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| PUT | `/api/articles/{id}` | Required |

Same body fields as [Create article](#create-article), plus:

| Field | Type | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `update_slug` | bool | When `true` the slug is regenerated from the title (default: `false` — existing URLs stay stable). |

> **Warning:** Omit `update_slug` (or set it to `false`) to keep the existing URL intact. Setting it to `true` will break any external links to the old URL.

**curl:**

```bash
curl -X PUT -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "title":     "Updated Title",
    "content":   "New content.",
    "ai_content_disclosure": "none",
    "published": true
  }' \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/articles/664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcdef
```

**Response 200:** updated article object.

