### List deleted articles (trash)

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET | `/api/articles/trash` | Required |

Deleting an article (via the admin UI, this API, or MCP) is always a soft delete — the article is hidden from every public and admin listing but kept in the database with a `deleted_at` timestamp for **60 days**, exactly like the admin *Articles → Trash* page. This endpoint returns that same set.

**Response:**

```json
{
  "total": 1,
  "retention_days": 60,
  "articles": [
    {
      "id":         "664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcdef",
      "title":      "Example Article",
      "slug":       "example-article",
      "deleted_at": "2025-06-10T08:00:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-06-10T08:00:00Z"
    }
  ]
}
```

**curl:**

```bash
curl -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/articles/trash
```

### Restore a deleted article

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| POST | `/api/articles/{id}/restore` | Required |

Undoes a soft delete, exactly like the "Restore" button on the admin trash page. Only articles still within the 60-day retention window can be restored.

```bash
curl -X POST -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/articles/664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcdef/restore
```

**Response 200:** the restored article object.
**Response 404:** `{"error":"A cikk nem található a lomtárban, vagy lejárt a visszaállítási időablak"}` — either the ID doesn't exist, the article isn't deleted, or the 60-day window has passed.

