## Categories

### List categories

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET | `/api/categories` | Required |

**Response:**

```json
{
  "total": 8,
  "categories": [
    {
      "id":            "664a000000000000000000bb",
      "name":          "Technology",
      "slug":          "technology",
      "description":   "Tech news and reviews",
      "icon":          "cpu",
      "og_image":      "https://cdn.example.com/category.png",
      "display_order": 1,
      "created_at":    "2025-01-01T00:00:00Z",
      "updated_at":    "2025-01-01T00:00:00Z",
      "article_count": 12,
      "deletable":     false
    }
  ]
}
```

`article_count` is the number of non-deleted articles (including drafts and scheduled ones)
currently referencing this category. `deletable` is `true` only when `article_count` is `0` —
see [Delete category](#delete-category).

### Get one category

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET | `/api/categories/{id}` | Required |

**Response 200:** single category object, including `article_count` and `deletable` as above.
**Response 404:** `{"error":"..."}`

### Create category

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| POST | `/api/categories` | Required |

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `name` | string | Yes | Slug is auto-generated from name (Hungarian accents handled). |
| `description` | string | | |
| `icon` | string | | Bootstrap Icons name without the `bi-` prefix, e.g. `cpu`. |
| `og_image` | string | | Public Open Graph image URL for the category page. |
| `display_order` | int | | Lower = shown first (default: `0`). |

```bash
curl -X POST -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"name":"Technology","icon":"cpu","og_image":"https://cdn.example.com/category.png","display_order":1}' \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/categories
```

**Response 201:** created category object.

### Update category

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| PUT | `/api/categories/{id}` | Required |

Same fields as Create. Slug is always regenerated from the updated name.

```bash
curl -X PUT -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"name":"Tech & Gadgets","icon":"cpu","display_order":1}' \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/categories/664a000000000000000000bb
```

**Response 200:** updated category object.

### Delete category

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| DELETE | `/api/categories/{id}` | Required |

> **Warning:** A category cannot be deleted while any non-deleted article still references it (by
> `category_id` or by its cached name), including drafts and scheduled articles. Reassign or delete
> those articles first.

```bash
curl -X DELETE -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/categories/664a000000000000000000bb
```

**Response 200:** `{"message": "..."}`.

**Response 409:** `resource_in_use`, including the referencing article count and a suggested action. Category follows are removed automatically and do not block deletion.

**Response 404:** category not found.

