## Pages

Custom static (evergreen) pages under `/admin/pages` — e.g. "About us" or "Service → Repairs" — fully manageable from a remote program the same way as articles. Pages are hierarchical via `parent_id` and each has a unique `path` (the full URL path, without a leading slash and without the optional `PAGE_URL_PREFIX`).

### List pages

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET | `/api/pages` | Required |

**Query parameters:**

- `published` — `true` to return only published pages; omit for all

**Response:**

```json
{
  "total": 2,
  "pages": [
    {
      "id":              "664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcd10",
      "title":           "Service",
      "slug":             "szerviz",
      "path":             "szerviz",
      "parent_id":        null,
      "layout":           "default",
      "content":          "Markdown content…",
      "summary":          "Short summary…",
      "seo_title":        "",
      "seo_description":  "",
      "og_image":         "",
      "published":        true,
      "published_at":     "2025-06-01T10:00:00Z",
      "menu_order":       0,
      "show_in_nav":      true,
      "created_at":       "2025-06-01T09:55:00Z",
      "updated_at":       "2025-06-01T09:55:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id":              "664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcd11",
      "title":           "Repairs",
      "slug":             "javitas",
      "path":             "szerviz/javitas",
      "parent_id":        "664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcd10",
      "layout":           "default",
      "published":        true,
      "menu_order":       0,
      "show_in_nav":      false
    }
  ]
}
```

**curl:**

```bash
curl -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" \
  "{{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/pages?published=true"
```

### Get one page

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET | `/api/pages/{id}` | Required |

`{id}` is the MongoDB ObjectID (24-char hex string).

**Response 200:** page object (same shape as in list).
**Response 404:** `{"error":"Az oldal nem található"}`

```bash
curl -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/pages/664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcd11
```

### Get a page by URL path

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET | `/api/pages/by-path?path={path}` | Required |

Looks a page up by its canonical URL path instead of its ObjectID — the same lookup the public site uses to serve a page. `{path}` is the full path without a leading slash and without `PAGE_URL_PREFIX` (e.g. `szerviz/javitas`), URL-encoded as a query parameter. Useful when a remote program knows a page's URL but not its ID.

**Response 200:** page object.
**Response 400:** missing `path` parameter.
**Response 404:** `{"error":"Az oldal nem található"}`

```bash
curl -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" \
  "{{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/pages/by-path?path=szerviz/javitas"
```

### Create page

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| POST | `/api/pages` | Required |

**Request body (JSON):**

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `title` | string | Yes | |
| `slug` | string | | Auto-generated from `title` when omitted; must be unique among siblings under the same parent. |
| `content` | string | | Markdown body. |
| `summary` | string | | |
| `layout` | string | | One of `default`, `landing`, `sidebar`, `wide`, `plain`, `sidebar-plain`. |
| `parent_id` | string | | ObjectID of an existing page; omit or empty for a top-level page. |
| `seo_title` / `seo_description` / `og_image` | string | | |
| `published` | bool | | |
| `publish_at` | string (RFC3339) | | Optional scheduled publish time. |
| `menu_order` | int | | Ordering among sibling pages. |
| `show_in_nav` | bool | | Only relevant for top-level pages. |

```bash
curl -X POST -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "title": "Repairs",
    "content": "## Service and repairs\n\nContact us for a quote.",
    "parent_id": "664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcd10",
    "published": true,
    "show_in_nav": false
  }' \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/pages
```

**Response 201:** created page object.

### Update page

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| PUT | `/api/pages/{id}` | Required |

Same fields as Create.

> **Note:** The slug (and therefore `path`) only changes when `update_slug: true` is sent — otherwise the existing URL stays stable even if `title` changes. Changing `parent_id` cascades the new `path` down to every descendant page.

```bash
curl -X PUT -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"title":"Repairs","content":"Updated content.","published":true}' \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/pages/664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcd11
```

**Response 200:** updated page object.

### Delete page

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| DELETE | `/api/pages/{id}` | Required |

> **Warning:** A page with children cannot be deleted — remove or re-parent its child pages first. The response is `409 Conflict` with `resource_in_use` and a `child_page` dependency otherwise.

```bash
curl -X DELETE -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/pages/664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcd11
```

**Response 200:** `{"message":"Az oldal sikeresen törölve"}`

