## Polls

Management endpoints for remotely creating and administering polls, the same way a remote program manages articles or authors. These are separate from the public `GET /api/polls/{id}` and `POST /api/polls/{id}/vote` endpoints, which use a logged-in portal user's session (not an API key) and power the poll widget embedded in articles — see `docs/polls.md` for embedding and voting.

### List polls

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET | `/api/polls/manage` | Required |

**Query parameters:**

- `status` — `draft`, `active`, `closed` or `archived`; omit for all polls

**Response:**

```json
{
  "total": 2,
  "polls": [
    {
      "id":          "664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcd01",
      "title":       "Which feature should we build next?",
      "description": "Optional context shown above the options.",
      "options": [
        { "id": "664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcd02", "text": "Dark mode" },
        { "id": "664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcd03", "text": "RSS reader" }
      ],
      "mode":         "single",
      "min_choices":  1,
      "max_choices":  1,
      "status":       "active",
      "starts_at":    null,
      "ends_at":      "2025-07-01T12:00:00Z",
      "created_at":   "2025-06-01T09:55:00Z",
      "updated_at":   "2025-06-01T09:55:00Z"
    }
  ]
}
```

**curl:**

```bash
curl -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" \
  "{{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/polls/manage?status=active"
```

### Get one poll

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET | `/api/polls/manage/{id}` | Required |

`{id}` is the MongoDB ObjectID (24-char hex string).

**Response 200:** single poll object (same shape as in list), including vote counts are *not* included here — use the admin results page for tallies.
**Response 404:** `{"error":"A szavazás nem található"}`

```bash
curl -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/polls/manage/664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcd01
```

### Create poll

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| POST | `/api/polls/manage` | Required |

**Request body (JSON):**

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `title` | string | Yes | Max 200 characters. |
| `description` | string | | Max 1000 characters. |
| `option_texts` | string[] | Yes | 2–50 unique, non-empty options (max 200 chars each). |
| `mode` | string | Yes | `single` or `multiple`. |
| `min_choices` / `max_choices` | int | | Only used when `mode` is `multiple`; ignored (forced to 1/1) for `single`. |
| `status` | string | Yes | Initial status: `draft` or `active`. |
| `starts_at` | string (RFC3339) | | Optional scheduled start; omit to allow voting immediately once active. |
| `ends_at` | string (RFC3339) | Yes | Must be in the future and after `starts_at`. |

```bash
curl -X POST -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "title": "Which feature should we build next?",
    "option_texts": ["Dark mode", "RSS reader"],
    "mode": "single",
    "status": "draft",
    "ends_at": "2025-07-01T12:00:00Z"
  }' \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/polls/manage
```

**Response 201:** created poll object.
**Response 400:** validation error, e.g. `{"error":"poll must have 2 to 50 options"}`

### Update poll

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| PUT | `/api/polls/manage/{id}` | Required |

Same fields as Create.

> **Warning:** Once a poll has received at least one vote, its options, `mode` and `min_choices`/`max_choices` are locked — only `title`, `description`, `starts_at` and `ends_at` may still change. Attempting to change locked fields returns **409 Conflict**.

```bash
curl -X PUT -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "title": "Which feature should we build next? (updated)",
    "option_texts": ["Dark mode", "RSS reader"],
    "mode": "single",
    "status": "active",
    "ends_at": "2025-07-15T12:00:00Z"
  }' \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/polls/manage/664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcd01
```

**Response 200:** updated poll object.
**Response 409:** structure is locked after the first vote.

### Set status

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| POST | `/api/polls/manage/{id}/status` | Required |

**Request body (JSON):** `{"status": "active" | "closed" | "archived"}`

Valid transitions mirror the admin panel's poll actions:

- `draft` → `active` (only while `ends_at` is still in the future)
- `active` → `closed`
- `closed` or an expired `active` poll → `archived`

```bash
curl -X POST -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"status":"active"}' \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/polls/manage/664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcd01/status
```

**Response 200:** updated poll object.
**Response 409:** invalid transition for the poll's current state.

### Delete poll

| Method | URL | Auth |
| --- | --- | --- |
| DELETE | `/api/polls/manage/{id}` | Required |

> **Note:** Only `draft` polls with no votes can be deleted — close or archive a poll instead of deleting it once it has gone live.

```bash
curl -X DELETE -H "X-API-Key: {{if .APIKey}}{{.APIKey}}{{else}}YOUR_KEY{{end}}" \
  {{if .SiteURL}}{{.SiteURL}}{{else}}https://example.com{{end}}/api/polls/manage/664a1b2c3d4e5f6789abcd01
```

**Response 200:** `{"message":"A szavazás sikeresen törölve"}`.
**Response 409:** the poll is not a vote-free draft.
